From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:48:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 4655 (tester 55954): two requests in one sentence are judged
 apart
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Gelas hkitkhe, khom ar icis kargi santeknikosi, da Levans stkhove,
gamacnos Nino." is one sentence with two requests; 0195 judged each person
by the sentence they are named in, so Gela sat in the introduction's
sentence and every ask to him was refused. A comma followed by
da/asevе/and/also, or a semicolon, now starts the next person's part; a
bare "da" splits nothing, so "gamacani Nino da Giorgi" stays one
introduction. No new text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
